            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0470" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.643/50: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-25T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>287. Your 653, August 24, noon.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d326-f1"/> The Department’s
                    desire is that the return of the consular premises in Nanking and any ceremonies
                    attendant thereon shall take place as soon as possible without awaiting
                    completion of repairs. See Department’s 273, August 17, 6 p.m., paragraph 1, and
                    281, August 21, 8 p.m., paragraph 2, regarding temporary quarters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
